.TH tkutlstate n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutlstate
.PP
Save and restore a \fBtablelist\fR's column layout \(em widths, hidden state,
display order and the active sort \(em so an application can persist how the
user arranged a table.
.SS Commands
.CS
::tkutils::tkutlstate::save            tbl
::tkutils::tkutlstate::restore         tbl state
::tkutils::tkutlstate::saveToFile      tbl path
::tkutils::tkutlstate::restoreFromFile tbl path
.CE
.PP
The state is a plain Tcl dict (text\-storable). \fBrestore\fR only touches
columns present in both the saved state and the current table, so it degrades
gracefully when the table changed.
.SS Example
.CS
::tkutils::tkutlstate::saveToFile .t $cfg
::tkutils::tkutlstate::restoreFromFile .t $cfg
.CE
.SS "Error codes"
\fB\-errorcode {TKUTILS TKUTLSTATE STATE}\fR for a non\-state value.
.SH KEYWORDS
tablelist, persistence, columns, layout
